      "settings": {
        "hero_title": "Understanding Diamonds: The 4 C's",
        "hero_intro": "<p>Diamonds are extraordinary natural materials, formed under immense heat and pressure and valued for their exceptional hardness, brilliance and ability to interact with light. Yet two diamonds of the same size can differ considerably in appearance, rarity and value. Understanding the 4 C's:  Cut, Colour, Clarity and Carat Weight, gives you a practical framework for recognising those differences and comparing stones more confidently. Each characteristic contributes something different: cut influences brilliance and sparkle, colour measures how colourless a white diamond appears, clarity considers its natural internal and external characteristics, and carat describes its weight. The key is not simply to pursue the highest grade in every category, but to understand how these factors work together to create a diamond that balances beauty, quality, individuality and value.</p>",
        "callout_bg_color": "#f7f5f3",
